# The C++ style of src/main/cpp and src/test/cpp: LLVM, with wider lines and four-space indentation.
# Enforced in CI with a pinned clang-format (.github/workflows/clang-format.yml); `clang-format
# --dump-config` lists every option this resolves to.
---
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
ColumnLimit: 120
IndentWidth: 4
# Attributes stay on the line of what they annotate: `[[nodiscard]] inline std::string f()`.
BreakAfterAttributes: Never
# Include order is load-bearing and kept by hand: the upstream server headers define the `json` alias
# that json_helpers.hpp and jni_helpers.hpp use, so they have to come first (CLAUDE.md, "Code Formatting").
SortIncludes: Never
...
